{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms","id":1362082,"title":"Dragon-blooded Charm vs Solar Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-20T04:30:25-08:00","id":1362082,"title":"Dragon-blooded Charm vs Solar Charms","content":"I'm doing a new post because Lioness (I think ?) suggested to try to to more new topics instead of asking everything on Ask a question, get an answer.<br /> <br /> I guess there has been a topic about this in the past, but did anyone do a comparison between Solar Charms and Dragon-blooded from an ergonomic point of view ? I feel like Solars have more Charms, but I also know a lot of them are only dice tricks, or poorly designed in relation to the other Charms in regards to the number total number of Charms.<br /> <br /> How is it going for Dragon-Blooded ? I have played DB only once, and it was quite fun. I felt like I had less options at hand, but I also felt like I had less &quot;filler&quot; Charms, even though they were less powerful than Solar's, they seemed to serve a clearer purpose to me. There were dice tricks as well, and I still don't know what I think of them : In a game where you can roll between 15 and 30 dices, and quite regularly can go over 10 successes, what do I think of dice tricks ? I accepted them more for Dragon-Blooded because I knew they were needed if I wanted to come closer to Solar prowesses, but I think this is misconception on my part because I'm used to Solar results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T06:15:01-08:00","id":1362091,"title":"","content":"Solars definitely have more charms and more ability to combine charms. So you can do things like fire off a combo with ten different charms enhancing it and do crazy things that send the numbers through the roof. As you grow your ability to make those crazy numbers happen gets bigger and bigger. <br /> <br /> With Dragonblooded it\u2019s more like a toolbox of different abilities. A lot of them are simple or restricted by Aura and so can\u2019t combine together very much. On the other hand a much greater percentage of them do things that are big flashy effects or just unlock an ability that you couldn\u2019t even attempt before. That way as you grow in power your toolbox gets bigger and bigger.<br /> <br /> I personally like it a lot, they\u2019re both good ways to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T06:39:36-08:00","id":1362096,"title":"","content":"Probably worth noting that &quot;Dragon blooded have less charms&quot; isn't supposed to be true in-universe. It's just a product of wordcount constraints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T07:01:39-08:00","id":1362103,"title":"","content":"I think it was also a design choice. The sheer size of many of the Solar trees is pretty daunting. The DB ones are fairly large still and are getting expansions in Heirs to the Shogunate as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:04:50-08:00","id":1362111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362091#post1362091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars definitely have more charms and more ability to combine charms. So you can do things like fire off a combo with ten different charms enhancing it and do crazy things that send the numbers through the roof. As you grow your ability to make those crazy numbers happen gets bigger and bigger.<br /> <br /> With Dragonblooded it\u2019s more like a toolbox of different abilities. A lot of them are simple or restricted by Aura and so can\u2019t combine together very much. On the other hand a much greater percentage of them do things that are big flashy effects or just unlock an ability that you couldn\u2019t even attempt before. That way as you grow in power your toolbox gets bigger and bigger.<br /> <br /> I personally like it a lot, they\u2019re both good ways to go about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>When discovering them Solar Charms makes you feel like you have infinite possibility, but with more time I find myself annoyed by a huge amount of Charms that use mechanically complex ways of saying &quot;You roll more dices&quot;. I didn't feel like this when playing DB, which was quite good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:23:49-08:00","id":1362116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362111#post1362111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When discovering them Solar Charms makes you feel like you have infinite possibility, but with more time I find myself annoyed by a huge amount of Charms that use mechanically complex ways of saying &amp;quot;You roll more dices&amp;quot;. I didn't feel like this when playing DB, which was quite good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I generally prefer it as well. It\u2019s slightly less concerned with raw power and charm interactions and more focused on just doing cool shit. The signature charms especially, become a living tangle of brambles, breathe fire, fly, redirect attacks at foes, melt into stone ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:28:08-08:00","id":1362117,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think there is something amiss around there in the Solar Charms. We can still home-brew Charms of course, but I wouldn't be against a simple framework for how to make cool Charms for Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:56:17-08:00","id":1362244,"title":"","content":"On &quot;Does cool shit&quot; vs &quot;More dice&quot; I wonder how much of how much of that is wholly intentional vs core devs initially planning for Evocations and Sorcery to do more heavy lifting on those aspects, and Charms not so much needing to? And whether the design would end up the same in retrospect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:26:01-08:00","id":1362281,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not a dev but I think the Solars more dice is, essentially, their cool shit. They don\u2019t have an athletics charm that lets them rush an enemy while igniting a blazing line of bonfire all along their path that burns their foes, but they have a charm that lets them attempt any feat of strength, no matter how big, and do so with double 7s AND rerolling all failed dice. So they can grab a ten foot thick fortress wall and tear it down with their bare hands in a single action and Dragonblooded just can\u2019t do that.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded have a flashy brawl charm that gives them a huge watery tentacle exo-body thing that gives them a huge plethora of abilities, but a Solar brawler can grapple and shake a creature the size of Juggernaut, and DBs can\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T18:13:42-08:00","id":1362290,"title":"","content":"I agree that Solars being able to get sky-high successes is their coolness. Winning is the theme, after all.<br /> <br /> My Dragon-Blooded game has the players using Dragon-Blooded Charms quite a bit, and I get the impression they like the flavor of the different Excellencies. We're not Essence 3 yet, so no signatures. However, it's a warstrider game, so most of the distinctiveness is in their Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T18:30:56-08:00","id":1362295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362244#post1362244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On &quot;Does cool shit&quot; vs &quot;More dice&quot; I wonder how much of how much of that is wholly intentional vs core devs initially planning for Evocations and Sorcery to do more heavy lifting on those aspects, and Charms not so much needing to? And whether the design would end up the same in retrospect?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm almost certain this was at least part of the ideal and it even fits solar's to a T with their universal Resonant ability with Artifacts and being able to achieve the highest highs in Sorcery. And as I've discovered, a single lore character with <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wake the Sleeper open A LOT of nifty unique powers for them.<br /> <br /> Honestly the real issues with Solar charms at times is that some abilities don't really care about </span>threshold<span style=\"font-size:13px\"> successes as much as others.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T20:26:50-08:00","id":1362326,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the tight, concise Charm trees of DBs and the various angles they approach their Ability from. DB Bureaucracy is one of my favorite trees because it feels like a really interesting stage for the elements' different personalities to shine. Also because I just like Bureaucracy as an ability even if the Solar tree doesn't feel especially exciting. And then there's Wind-Carried Words Technique, aka Glorious Terrestrial Cellphone, which is wonderful.<br /> <br /> I also think one big change in the old devs/new devs split that at least slightly exacerbates Solar charm tree enormity compared to others is that what the old devs would split into separately-named, separately-listed charms, the new devs seem more likely to format as automatic charm upgrades or higher-requirement repurchases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T08:02:38-08:00","id":1362653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362281#post1362281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not a dev but I think the Solars more dice is, essentially, their cool shit. They don\u2019t have an athletics charm that lets them rush an enemy while igniting a blazing line of bonfire all along their path that burns their foes, but they have a charm that lets them attempt any feat of strength</div> </div> </div> </div>But Solar Athletics DOES have a Charm for substituting a normal rush action with &quot;I am instantly at close range with you, and I get to make an enhanced attack as well&quot;, as well as a Charm for &quot;I get to make a normal rush action against you from outside the usual range for a rush action, and also I get TWO reflexive advances on you instead of one&quot;.<br /> <br /> THAT is &quot;do cool shit&quot; rather than &quot;moar dice&quot;.<br /> <br /> Solars get their own tricks for breaking the universal rules of the game, on top of many dice tricks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T08:26:21-08:00","id":1362654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362653#post1362653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Solar Athletics DOES have a Charm for substituting a normal rush action with &quot;I am instantly at close range with you, and I get to make an enhanced attack as well&quot;, as well as a Charm for &quot;I get to make a normal rush action against you from outside the usual range for a rush action, and also I get TWO reflexive advances on you instead of one&quot;.<br /> <br /> THAT is &quot;do cool shit&quot; rather than &quot;moar dice&quot;.<br /> <br /> Solars get their own tricks for breaking the universal rules of the game, on top of many dice tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's really the kind of Charms I would like to see more in Solar. I already home-brew a good part of the Charms when I find them too weak or uninteresting but mandatory for players that they can buy a pack for a reduced cost because well, it's not fun for the player either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T09:17:47-08:00","id":1362666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362653#post1362653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Solar Athletics DOES have a Charm for substituting a normal rush action with &quot;I am instantly at close range with you, and I get to make an enhanced attack as well&quot;, as well as a Charm for &quot;I get to make a normal rush action against you from outside the usual range for a rush action, and also I get TWO reflexive advances on you instead of one&quot;.<br /> <br /> THAT is &quot;do cool shit&quot; rather than &quot;moar dice&quot;.<br /> <br /> Solars get their own tricks for breaking the universal rules of the game, on top of many dice tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, and every exalt type has charms for adding more dice, at the very least they have excellencies for every action it\u2019s not totally exclusive. Even their charms that aren\u2019t just flat more dice tend towards just making that action better or more efficient or enhancing the scope in some way. They have an athletics charm to double damage, but not one to create a wide range environmental hazard that knocks targets back and prone with a big fiery shockwave. <br /> <br /> Again, not exclusively true there\u2019s some really out there charms, but considering the staggering size of the Solar charmset compared to the DB one the DBs have way fewer charms that enhance an action.<br /> <br /> Edit: if we\u2019re considering things like One More Step and Living Wind Approach to be \u201cdo cool shit\u201d charms then I can\u2019t agree with Chausse that Solars don\u2019t have a lot of them, they have literally hundreds of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-22-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T10:39:06-08:00","id":1362679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362666#post1362666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, and every exalt type has charms for adding more dice, at the very least they have excellencies for every action it\u2019s not totally exclusive. Even their charms that aren\u2019t just flat more dice tend towards just making that action better or more efficient or enhancing the scope in some way. They have an athletics charm to double damage, but not one to create a wide range environmental hazard that knocks targets back and prone with a big fiery shockwave.<br /> <br /> Again, not exclusively true there\u2019s some really out there charms, but considering the staggering size of the Solar charmset compared to the DB one the DBs have way fewer charms that enhance an action.<br /> <br /> Edit: if we\u2019re considering things like One More Step and Living Wind Approach to be \u201cdo cool shit\u201d charms then I can\u2019t agree with Chausse that Solars don\u2019t have a lot of them, they have literally hundreds of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my stance is rather than they have Charms that do cool shit, but there are too many Charms that are boring dice tricks as well (or contain boring dice tricks that just changes the motes calculation for nothing), and some of them are pre requisite as well (Craft is of course the worst offender, but it's not the only one). My initial post was to ask wether Dragon-Blooded were more spared from that, which you confirmed they were. <br /> <br /> My philosophy about &quot;efficiency&quot; Charms would be that it's fine to have them, if there are few of them and their impact is direct and effective for the player : Gain a Free Full excellency on ability one per scene is cool and you easily remember it, but Umbral eye &quot;You gain 1 automatic successes and 2 dices for 2 motes on a roll to specifically read intentions about a character for which you created or changed an intimacy&quot; is way too specific. Gain +3 Guilde in permanence is cool and clear and written on your sheet in a memorable way, but Winning Stride discipline that gives you 2 motes or 2 initiative only for Athletics when you successfully win a test of speed but that is not the same Charm that Onrush Burst Method which gives you 3 motes (and not initiative) for Athletics Charms but only on a Rush action and not in a test of speed and bzzzz. I can assure you when you play someone with Athletics supernal these Charms are the worst to be paid, you just forget them because meanwhile you have 8 different other Charms with real effect on the game that you have to take into account when you rush and attack someone.<br /> <br /> So I might be slightly accentuating the problem of dice tricks (because they are not the majority of Charms, thanks God), but I was really glad when I played Dragon Blooded and felt much more ease to use their Charms, except for the excellency that I think they should have all unified to avoid checking &quot;What's the special effect of Athletics Excellency already ?&quot; with something like &quot;Dragon Blooded always reroll 6&quot; or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T10:57:45-08:00","id":1362682,"title":"","content":"Part of that is probably the size too. Solars have like 1,000 charms or something and with so many it\u2019s hard to make each one a big unique memorable effect. It\u2019s easier to make a character that has a super hard focus on one ability though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T11:06:12-08:00","id":1362685,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think as well that the number of Charms, coupled with the absence of a Charm tree to allow the player to easily visualise what is going on, is a lackluster.<br /> <br /> But for Athletics, I think they managed to make really unique memorable effect, when they are not about small dice/mote tricks : Graceful Crane Stance, Monkey Leap, Soaring Crane Leap, Foe Vaulting, Increasing Strength, Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Feather Foot, Spider Foot, and they all are only Essence 1 Charms, and every one of them is either simple, effective of use cleverly the established mechanics of the game to put a twist on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T11:08:31-08:00","id":1362686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362666#post1362666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if we\u2019re considering things like One More Step and Living Wind Approach to be \u201cdo cool shit\u201d charms then I can\u2019t agree with Chausse that Solars don\u2019t have a lot of them, they have literally hundreds of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean to say so.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to argue Solars don't have too many dice-effects.<br /> <br /> I only meant to point out that there's a core of &quot;do cool shit&quot; effects in the Solar Charmset, and I suppose those could shine more if there were fewer Solar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T11:32:12-08:00","id":1362691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362653#post1362653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Solar Athletics DOES have a Charm for substituting a normal rush action with &quot;I am instantly at close range with you, and I get to make an enhanced attack as well&quot;, as well as a Charm for &quot;I get to make a normal rush action against you from outside the usual range for a rush action, and also I get TWO reflexive advances on you instead of one&quot;.<br /> <br /> THAT is &quot;do cool shit&quot; rather than &quot;moar dice&quot;.<br /> <br /> Solars get their own tricks for breaking the universal rules of the game, on top of many dice tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Solar Athletics tree is actually in rather good shape, as well as most of the combat-related abilities. The worst offender here are for me all Solar social trees, especially Linguistics and Socialise, I guess. They have so few actual effects and they are so terribly focused on stacking minor bonuses. I mean, if it were at least double 9s, that would be bearable, but most of them are slight discounts on excellencies.<br /> <br /> The original devs were clearly afraid of social charms becoming too potent and the result is that they barely do anything for most of the time.<br /> <br /> Seriously, after seeing Dragon-Blooded and Lunars, I would really pay to see Exalted revised Solar book, where just the charmset is slightly ironed. Even the difference between the core book and Miracles is already striking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T11:56:09-08:00","id":1362695,"title":"","content":"I do agree that some of the Solar charm sets are much better for doing distinct things. Athletics,* Larceny, Investigation, most of the combat abilities, . While Presence, Performance, Socialise, Linguistics and Craft are chock-full of excellency discounts and dice tricks. Oh, and craft point discounts. I think Presence is the worst, especially the bottom half of the tree, though I haven't gone through and compared exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I actually think Athletics is the most poorly-written of the charmsets, but it is full of cool stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T12:13:35-08:00","id":1362700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362686#post1362686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean to say so.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to argue Solars don't have too many dice-effects.<br /> <br /> I only meant to point out that there's a core of &amp;quot;do cool shit&amp;quot; effects in the Solar Charmset, and I suppose those could shine more if there were fewer Solar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, 100% with you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T12:26:48-08:00","id":1362705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362695#post1362695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Presence is the worst, especially the bottom half of the tree, though I haven't gone through and compared exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, there are a couple of good charms. Tiger's Dreadful Symmetry or Listener's Swaying Argument are ok. But I can't help thinking that most of them are basically just a tax on Hypnotic Tongue Technique. I wonder whether it wouldn't be healthier just to make some charms more expansive because of their clear utility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-22-2020, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T13:59:08-08:00","id":1362723,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, there's no charmsets with nothing good in at all. But Presence has a lot of marginal stuff in as well.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I dislike Listener-Swaying Argument, but I'll admit it's a strong charm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-22-2020, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T14:06:37-08:00","id":1362726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362705#post1362705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, there are a couple of good charms. Tiger's Dreadful Symmetry or Listener's Swaying Argument are ok. But I can't help thinking that most of them are basically just a tax on Hypnotic Tongue Technique. I wonder whether it wouldn't be healthier just to make some charms more expansive because of their clear utility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Variable charm price is probably something to consider for 4th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T00:49:25-08:00","id":1362816,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think people underlined perfectly that some trees are in a better state than others. I didn't notice it was social trees that had more &quot;problematic&quot; designs, but now that people talked about it it seems more obvious. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking about changing some of them to an extent. I usually do not feel bad removing dice adders Charms/dice tricks Charms (because Solars have free Excellencies), and I'd like to replace them with simple generic effect that people easily remember they have and is rather straightforward. For the moment, these strike me as obvious : <br /> - Free full excellency once per scene (usually around Essence 2)<br /> - Double 9 (around Essence 1 or 2 usually)<br /> <br /> Are there others ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T01:09:37-08:00","id":1362821,"title":"","content":"Rerolls, Rerolls, but where you keep the better result, cascading 10's. Penalising the oponnent's 1s. Situational non-charm dice (I don't know whether these count as dice tricks). Cascading rerolls of 6s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T01:43:59-08:00","id":1362823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362821#post1362821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rerolls, Rerolls, but where you keep the better result, cascading 10's. Penalising the oponnent's 1s. Situational non-charm dice (I don't know whether these count as dice tricks). Cascading rerolls of 6s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think each of these effect is worth an entire Charm ? I know there are Charms in the books that just do this, but they are usually part of the &quot;I'm not sure they are worth their cost&quot; Charms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T02:04:37-08:00","id":1362825,"title":"","content":"It really depends. If you're regularly opposing Exalts with massive dice pools, they're worth the xp. Otherwise, your free excellency is fine. In fact, the excellency is a better charm than a lot of them (not all), and you should only use them if you've already maxed out your excellency.<br /> <br /> There are others that are basically just discounted excellencies, and I suppose saving motes is worth a charm for some characters.<br /> <br /> I do feel a lot of them are marginal enough that they should really not be at the base of trees though. If you're the sort of player who carefully keeps their essence expenditure down, then a charm that gives Diuble 9s for 4m is something you are not going to use (as you could instead buy 4 more dice, which on a 10 dice pool is better).<br /> Similarly, charms to reduce mote costs of your excellencies are something that you don't need until later, because at character gen you may not have many charms to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T03:15:46-08:00","id":1362830,"title":"","content":"Yeah, some charms seem to be for wringing one or two additional successes out of an already maxed dice pool. if you use them before that point the motes are probably better spent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> There's a weird paradox where higher ability charms can get away with being less good than lower ability ones cos lower ability charms need to be better than just buying another dot of the ability, but ability 5 prerequisite charms don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T04:18:57-08:00","id":1362841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362825#post1362825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really depends. If you're regularly opposing Exalts with massive dice pools, they're worth the xp. Otherwise, your free excellency is fine. In fact, the excellency is a better charm than a lot of them (not all), and you should only use them if you've already maxed out your excellency.<br /> <br /> There are others that are basically just discounted excellencies, and I suppose saving motes is worth a charm for some characters.<br /> <br /> I do feel a lot of them are marginal enough that they should really not be at the base of trees though. If you're the sort of player who carefully keeps their essence expenditure down, then a charm that gives Diuble 9s for 4m is something you are not going to use (as you could instead buy 4 more dice, which on a 10 dice pool is better).<br /> Similarly, charms to reduce mote costs of your excellencies are something that you don't need until later, because at character gen you may not have many charms to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking only from an &quot;statistical efficiency&quot; point of view, but also from from an easier management from the player's perspective : so many dice trick Charms have so many different dice trick rules it makes them impossible to track quickly, wether they be efficient or not.<br /> <br /> Here's a suggestion of what I would like people interested to help make me build :<br /> <br /> <b>Solar mastery </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Essence : 1 (Repurchase at 2 and 3). Abilities : Those concerned by annoying dice tricks, Socialize, Presence, Performance, Linguistics, Lore also I believe, but some others are offenders as well.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cost : 2m</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blabla Lawgiver blabla truth of the sun blabla shining light. You gain Double 9 on the roll. You get one free Full Excellency once per scene.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Repurchase (Essence 2) : You gain cascading 10s on a roll. You can reroll once per scene and keep the better result.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Repurchase (Essence 3) : (Permanent) Your maximum Excellency cost is capped at 6. You can double 8s once per scene.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Please keep in mind the purpose of this Charm would be to replace every dice trick Charms in a given tree. The only Charms left would be either those with a direct effect, or those whose subsystem is so specific they cannot me changed (like Athletics and Feats of Strength, or the Crafting system). The purpose here is to consider that Excellency is actually the base Mechanism for dice tricks, because it literally allows more dices to be thrown, which I believe is enough for the players to care about. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">They are in 3 tiers, they unlock 3 different and generic powers that are kinda recurrent across the Solar Charms tree : Double 9 and Free Full excellency, Cascading 10s and reroll, Mote economy and Double 8s. <br /> <br /> The idea is, you know which tier you have then you know your exacts dice tricks, and there are no others. I tried to mix effects that were weak but core to solar ideas with other stronger power so the overall cost of (re)purchase is worth a Charm.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you pay this Charm for each concerned ability.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T05:55:29-08:00","id":1362859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362841#post1362841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not asking only from an &quot;statistical efficiency&quot; point of view, but also from from an easier management from the player's perspective : so many dice trick Charms have so many different dice trick rules it makes them impossible to track quickly, wether they be efficient or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true.<br /> <br /> I tend to write seperately on my sheet some common ways to make rolls, like so (this is from my Full Moon):<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Combat tactics (Stunt bonuses are 1pt, and included)</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Join Battle</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 8 dice</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boosted Join Battle</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 5m for 13 dice</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ultimate Join Battle: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">10m for 13 dice, reroll 1s and double 9s. (The re-roll 1s is until they no longer appear.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ultimate Join Battle with a stunt: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">15m for 20 dice, re-roll 1s and double 9s. (The re-roll 1s is until they no longer appear.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Withering Attack</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 3 motes. 15 dice, re-roll up to 5 failures. +12 damage (14 with Essence-Fangs active). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mighty Withering Attack</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 11 motes. 20 dice +1 success, re-roll up to 5 failures, roll an extra dice for each 10. +14 damage (16 with Essence-Fangs active). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ultimate Withering Attack with stunt vs an enemy with lower initiative or who hasn't had their turn</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 19 motes. 27 dice +1 success, re-roll up to 5 failures, roll an extra dice for each 10. +19 damage (21 with Essence-Fangs active). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Add 5m, 1wp to ignore soak from armour.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">If necessary, add 3m to re-roll up to five 1s and ignore 1pt from medium parry/cover/full defence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Poison decisive attack:</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 8 motes, 2i. 16 dice. With a stunt, 10 motes, 2i, for 23 dice.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Poison damage 2i/round (A in Crash), Duration 6 rounds, \u20132 penalty. Or 1i(A), -4.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">For each 10 on the damage roll, add 1 to either duration, penalty or damage. Duration can't be reduced below 1.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">If necessary, add 3m to re-roll up to five 1s and ignore 1pt from medium parry/cover/full defence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Poison attack vs a crashed enemy</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 14 motes, 3i, 1wp. 16 dice. With a stunt, 19 motes, 3i, 1wp. for 23 dice. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Does +1 auto-success on the damage roll.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Poison damage 1 agg/round, -2 penalty. Duration is 1 per 2 dice of raw damage rolled, enemy doesn't get a roll to resist.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Defence (Enemies take -1 or -3 penalty to hit when in Snake form): </b><br /> Parry 6<br /> 4m for Parry 8.<br /> 10m for Parry 12 with a stunt.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ... Yes, I have found that as annoying and complex to run as it is to read. I'd like to avoid dice tricks with my next character, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T05:59:43-08:00","id":1362861,"title":"","content":"Yeah this a bit heavy indeed. Thanks for sharing that though, I like the idea of &quot;Do the thing/DO the ultimate thing/Do the ultimate thing ++&quot; it still makes things a bit better to follow, I'll suggest it in my next campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T06:51:53-08:00","id":1362873,"title":"","content":"I should say, that's an Essence 5 character, so it's somewhat of an extreme example, as she has like 50 charms. But I didn't even deliberately try and get loads of dice tricks or anything. And she's a Lunar; Solars have slightly more.<br /> <br /> Still, I have found it saves a ton of time writing it like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T08:28:53-08:00","id":1362895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362679#post1362679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but Winning Stride discipline that gives you 2 motes or 2 initiative only for Athletics when you successfully win a test of speed but that is not the same Charm that Onrush Burst Method which gives you 3 motes (and not initiative) for Athletics Charms but only on a Rush action and not in a test of speed and bzzzz. I can assure you when you play someone with Athletics supernal these Charms are the worst to be paid, you just forget them because meanwhile you have 8 different other Charms with real effect on the game that you have to take into account when you rush and attack someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the only instance of the problem in Solar Athletics, either.<br /> <br /> Demon-Wasting Rush and Godspeed Steps both advance from Racing Hare Method. GS requires an additional Charm, but it's largely the superior Charm. Demon-Wasting Rush lets you rush from medium range, and gives you two reflexive movements. Godspeed Steps (which is actually slightly cheaper to use) not only allows you to rush from farther than Demon-Wasting Rush (especially if you're already using Racing Hare Method), except instead of rushing you automatically enter close range with your target, rendering the need for reflexive movements largely moot. Also, it removes the flurry penalty for ALSO attacking the target that turn.<br /> <br /> This seems to be an error of conflicting drafts. DWR is weak enough in comparison that it seems like it should have been a prerequisite for Godspeed Steps, but GS is so obviously superior that you'd never use Demon-Wasting Rush again except in very niche situations (such as your target having a Charm to reflexively escape close range without a disengage action). In being far more niche, DWR should follow after GS, but it's still not powerful enough within that specific niche to be worthwhile compared to Godspeed Steps.<br /> <br /> I also hear that Nine-Aeons Thew doesn't work as advertised, but I haven't experimented with Solar power-lifting Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I might be slightly accentuating the problem of dice tricks (because they are not the majority of Charms, thanks God), but I was really glad when I played Dragon Blooded and felt much more ease to use their Charms, except for the excellency that I think they should have all unified to avoid checking &quot;What's the special effect of Athletics Excellency already ?&quot; with something like &quot;Dragon Blooded always reroll 6&quot; or something like that. </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded Excellencies have specific effects because not all Abilities are made equal. Some benefit more from adding dice, others benefit more from adding successes, and some benefit too much from one effect, and others are so niche that they deserve to have effects which would be too powerful for more popular, frequently-used Abilities.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think that a lot of Solar dice-foolishness might have been avoided if Solars approached Excellencies the same way, the way they did in First Edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362682#post1362682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that is probably the size too. Solars have like 1,000 charms or something and with so many it\u2019s hard to make each one a big unique memorable effect. It\u2019s easier to make a character that has a super hard focus on one ability though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars being able to focus super-hard into one Ability was definitely a design goal, considering Supernal Abilities. It's a way to reinforce &quot;Solars have unparalleled talent within their areas of expertise&quot;, a way to distinguish different Solar Castes from each other, and a way to distinguish individual Solars from each other without elemental Aspects or Totem beasts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362685#post1362685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think as well that the number of Charms, coupled with the absence of a Charm tree to allow the player to easily visualise what is going on, is a lackluster.</div> </div> </div> </div>The staggering page-count of the book, together with the staggering number of Charms, might have made adding more pages for multiple Charm trees for every Ability somewhat unfeasible.<br /> <br /> But yes, I was also disappointed by the lack of that visual aid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But for Athletics, I think they managed to make really unique memorable effect, when they are not about small dice/mote tricks : Graceful Crane Stance, Monkey Leap, Soaring Crane Leap, Foe Vaulting, Increasing Strength, Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Feather Foot, Spider Foot, and they all are only Essence 1 Charms, and every one of them is either simple, effective of use cleverly the established mechanics of the game to put a twist on them. </div> </div> </div>&quot;They managed&quot; is perhaps inaccurate. These effects are a legacy of First Edition Core Book, not an invention of the men behind the Third Edition Core Book. They are instead more responsible for the Athletics Charms which tend to give us problems.<br /> <br /> Even the new version of the the old Monkey Leap Technique is not as neatly and clearly designed as I would like.<br /> <br /> I don't know what their circumstances were, so I don't wish to judge them based on the results of their work. In any case, it's in the past, and assigning blame doesn't fix the present problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-23-2020, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T08:46:26-08:00","id":1362899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362895#post1362895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the only instance of the problem in Solar Athletics, either.<br /> <br /> Demon-Wasting Rush and Godspeed Steps both advance from Racing Hare Method. GS requires an additional Charm, but it's largely the superior Charm. Demon-Wasting Rush lets you rush from medium range, and gives you two reflexive movements. Godspeed Steps (which is actually slightly cheaper to use) not only allows you to rush from farther than Demon-Wasting Rush (especially if you're already using Racing Hare Method), except instead of rushing you automatically enter close range with your target, rendering the need for reflexive movements largely moot. Also, it removes the flurry penalty for ALSO attacking the target that turn.<br /> <br /> This seems to be an error of conflicting drafts. DWR is weak enough in comparison that it seems like it should have been a prerequisite for Godspeed Steps, but GS is so obviously superior that you'd never use Demon-Wasting Rush again except in very niche situations (such as your target having a Charm to reflexively escape close range without a disengage action). In being far more niche, DWR should follow after GS, but it's still not powerful enough within that specific niche to be worthwhile compared to Godspeed Steps.<br /> <br /> I also hear that Nine-Aeons Thew doesn't work as advertised, but I haven't experimented with Solar power-lifting Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Excellencies have specific effects because not all Abilities are made equal. Some benefit more from adding dice, others benefit more from adding successes, and some benefit too much from one effect, and others are so niche that they deserve to have effects which would be too powerful for more popular, frequently-used Abilities.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think that a lot of Solar dice-foolishness might have been avoided if Solars approached Excellencies the same way, the way they did in First Edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Solars being able to focus super-hard into one Ability was definitely a design goal, considering Supernal Abilities. It's a way to reinforce &quot;Solars have unparalleled talent within their areas of expertise&quot;, a way to distinguish different Solar Castes from each other, and a way to distinguish individual Solars from each other without elemental Aspects or Totem beasts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The staggering page-count of the book, together with the staggering number of Charms, might have made adding more pages for multiple Charm trees for every Ability somewhat unfeasible.<br /> <br /> But yes, I was also disappointed by the lack of that visual aid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;They managed&quot; is perhaps inaccurate. These effects are a legacy of First Edition Core Book, not an invention of the men behind the Third Edition Core Book. They are instead more responsible for the Athletics Charms which tend to give us problems.<br /> <br /> Even the new version of the the old Monkey Leap Technique is not as neatly and clearly designed as I would like.<br /> <br /> I don't know what their circumstances were, so I don't wish to judge them based on the results of their work. In any case, it's in the past, and assigning blame doesn't fix the present problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how to divide in multiple quotes simply on this forum so I'll answer by paragraph.<br /> <br /> 1) I agree with you about these Charms, but the bigger problem is you can hardly fix them because they are not simple dice tricks, which is annoying.<br /> <br /> 2) I know different abilities do not benefit the same from successes and balance, but here we really on the opposite of simplicity. There is everything : Additional dice for every 10, reroll 6, add a success, add dices, add successes or dices as you wish, reroll a 1 specifically for every 10, add non Charms dice in case of full excellency.<br /> <br /> I mean ok these effects make the DB stronger &quot;technically&quot;, but I'd rather have a more unified solution than having a random effect on each different ability I have to check every time.<br /> <br /> 3 and 4 ) Nothing to say <br /> <br /> 5) I don't wish to judge or talk about the developers specifically. What I meant is that in this Edition (I don't know the others), the base Charms of Athletics are straightforward, memorable and cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T10:20:56-08:00","id":1362912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the only instance of the problem in Solar Athletics, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Athletics is full of awkwardly-written charms, things that don't interact well, etc.<br /> <br /> Although I do still agree with Chausse that it has loads of cool stuff.<br /> Which is annoying; I want to use Athletics because of all the cool stuff, but it's also full of awkwardness, mechanics-wise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean ok these effects make the DB stronger &quot;technically&quot;, but I'd rather have a more unified solution than having a random effect on each different ability I have to check every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not be as bad for PCs, but I've run a lot of DB NPCs, and it is irritating the way every single excellency is <i>slightly</i> different. Solars essentially start with 16 charms (15, plus an excellency which applies to a ton of different abilities), while DBs start with 20 that you have to remember; and charms being very similar but slightly different makes them harder to remember than stuff which is completely different. No-one gets Elemental Bolt and Wind-Carried Words mixed up, but off the top of my head I have no idea what the differences between the Lore and Linguistics excellencies are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still......<br /> This may sound like a trite answer, but Exalted: Essence should fix all these issues. I'm 100% sure Dragonblood will have identical excellencies for every ability, and I'm 99% sure both Solars and Dragonblood will have far less dice tricks and those dice tricks will be more similar and standardised. Maybe just doubles, for example, rather than re-rolling different numbers once or until they're gone, rolling extra dice for each 10, doubles, adding 1 success which reduces your dice-adding cap by 2, etc, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T11:23:55-08:00","id":1362919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362912#post1362912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may not be as bad for PCs, but I've run a lot of DB NPCs, and it is irritating the way every single excellency is <i>slightly</i> different. Solars essentially start with 16 charms (15, plus an excellency which applies to a ton of different abilities), while DBs start with 20 that you have to remember; and charms being very similar but slightly different makes them harder to remember than stuff which is completely different. No-one gets Elemental Bolt and Wind-Carried Words mixed up, but off the top of my head I have no idea what the differences between the Lore and Linguistics excellencies are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still......<br /> This may sound like a trite answer, but Exalted: Essence should fix all these issues. I'm 100% sure Dragonblood will have identical excellencies for every ability, and I'm 99% sure both Solars and Dragonblood will have far less dice tricks and those dice tricks will be more similar and standardised. Maybe just doubles, for example, rather than re-rolling different numbers once or until they're gone, rolling extra dice for each 10, doubles, adding 1 success which reduces your dice-adding cap by 2, etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even for PC's in my solo it was annoying. Every check called for opening the book, checking the excellency, etc ... Doesn't fit well.<br /> <br /> Yes I hope Exalted Essence will bring satisfying answers, and even hopefully, answers usable in the Core game, which would be good fixes. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't want to annoy people, but would just some of you give a quick thought about the post I made top of this page to propose a unifying Charm about all. Just to make sure I didn't do anything too wrong that would break of some specific balance inside the abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T12:15:26-08:00","id":1362929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362919#post1362919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even for PC's in my solo it was annoying. Every check called for opening the book, checking the excellency, etc ... Doesn't fit well.<br /> <br /> Yes I hope Exalted Essence will bring satisfying answers, and even hopefully, answers usable in the Core game, which would be good fixes.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't want to annoy people, but would just some of you give a quick thought about the post I made top of this page to propose a unifying Charm about all. Just to make sure I didn't do anything too wrong that would break of some specific balance inside the abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience was that most of them had effects that were easily shorthanded and put in the margin of the Abilities box on the sheet. For example, &quot;r6&quot; for rerolling 6s until none appear or &quot;!10&quot; for exploding 10s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T12:28:30-08:00","id":1362933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362929#post1362929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My experience was that most of them had effects that were easily shorthanded and put in the margin of the Abilities box on the sheet. For example, &amp;quot;r6&amp;quot; for rerolling 6s until none appear or &amp;quot;!10&amp;quot; for exploding 10s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do t suppose you could post the full list? Unless that was it. It sounds like a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T13:03:16-08:00","id":1362940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1362933#post1362933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do t suppose you could post the full list? Unless that was it. It sounds like a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never actually had a full list, since I only made shorthand for the Excellencies my characters had. Won't stop me from making one though! <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Archery: Wo dX, -dPEN visual obstruct Athletics: Fi sX, !10 Awareness: Ea d/sX Brawl: Wa cX, r6 damage Bureaucracy: Wa sX, r6 Craft: Ea dX, sxp for stunt Dodge: Fi sX, -allPEN environ Integrity: Ea sX, -1PEN wound/depriv/poison Investigation: Wa sX, r6 Larceny: Wa sX, mute Linguistics: Ai sX, r/10 Lore: Ai sX, @\u22654m: d9s fact Medicine: Wo dX, @max: +1 nC Sux Melee: Fi cX, -duel cost see book Occult: Ai dX, r/10 Performance: Wo sX, -allPEN multitarget Presence: Fi sX, !10 Resistance: Ea sX, r6 Ride: Wo sX, -1PEN barding Sail: Wa sX, r6 Socialize: Fi sX, mute Stealth: Ai sX, mute Survival: Wo sX, forage: +1manday/Sux Thrown: Ai dX, ignore Lcov, AirAu: ignore 1 Hcov War: Ea dX, r6</pre> </div>First two letters indicate the element. Next two indicate the type: dX is a die-adder, sX a success-adder, cX one of the combat excellencies that adds dice or defense. <br /> !10 is exploding 10s, r/10 is reroll a non-1 failure per 10, r6 is reroll 6s until they disappear. <br /> Everything else probably needs to be looked up once to understand what the hell the shorthand means but should serve as a memory aid thereafter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T14:22:35-08:00","id":1362952,"title":"","content":"I don't think the element matters, because I know all the elements for the Abilities (though some might not I guess) and it's balanced.<br /> <br /> I did it like this: <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Precision Observation Method</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Can buy dice or successes.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Stoking Bonfire Style</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Dice. If hit or parry, reduce cost by 1 vs that opponent for rest of scene. Stacks. Lost if attack/parry another enemy or miss/fail to parry.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Seeking Throw Technique</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Dice, ignore 1pt of cover or 2 if you aimed.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effortlessly Rising Flame</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Successes, also roll an extra non-charm dice for each 10)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Locquacious Courtier Technique</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Successes. Mute)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Audience-Enthusing Display</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Succeses. Ignore penalty for multiple targets.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Glowing Coal Radiance</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Successes, also roll an extra non-charm dice for each 10)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Distracting Breeze Meditation </b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Successes. Mute)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hidden Secrets Whisper</b></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (dice, re-roll non-1 failures for each 10.)</span><br /> <br /> It'd probably easier to replace the name with the Ability though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T02:29:31-08:00","id":1368013,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of playing an Essence 5 Dragonblood in... an Essence 5 Solars game. Yeah, crazy I know, but I can't think of any Solar or Lunar concepts I really like (I've been playing Exalted for 12 years, I think I'm a bit burnt out creatively).<br /> <br /> Any recommendations of Dragonblood charmsets that are worthwhile in a mixed game? I'm thinking Sail (just because we have no Solar sailor), but what else? Not much point trying to be the best combatant or best crafter, but what stuff could a Dragonblood be useful for that Solars are lacking in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T05:54:45-08:00","id":1368027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368013#post1368013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of playing an Essence 5 Dragonblood in... an Essence 5 Solars game. Yeah, crazy I know, but I can't think of any Solar or Lunar concepts I really like (I've been playing Exalted for 12 years, I think I'm a bit burnt out creatively).<br /> <br /> Any recommendations of Dragonblood charmsets that are worthwhile in a mixed game? I'm thinking Sail (just because we have no Solar sailor), but what else? Not much point trying to be the best combatant or best crafter, but what stuff could a Dragonblood be useful for that Solars are lacking in?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do the Solars in your game currently do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T06:43:36-08:00","id":1368034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368013#post1368013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much point trying to be the best combatant or best crafter, but what stuff could a Dragonblood be useful for that Solars are lacking in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why prioritise being the best, why not something because it has some tricks that look neat or to play out the quirks of sequencing things together?<br /> <br /> I mean, I would suggest Occult because you get to banish devils with magic exploding trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T08:52:24-08:00","id":1368051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368034#post1368034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why prioritise being the best, why not something because it has some tricks that look neat or to play out the quirks of sequencing things together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I shouldn't have used &quot;best&quot;. What I mean is about being useful to the group. I mean, I will take some combat stuff I think is cool, but no-one's going to go &quot;thank the Unconquered Sun we've got a combat-focused Dragonblood, or we'd be screwed!&quot; when most of the Solars are as good as a combat-focused Dragonblood, and one is much better.<br /> I don't want to feel like there's no reason for the other PCs to bother asking him to do anything, because they can do it better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, I would suggest Occult because you get to banish devils with magic exploding trees. </div> </div> </div>You can? Which charm is that?<br /> <br /> Although you did get me to go look and I found a charm for trapping spirits under a mountain for 5 centuries, which does seem cool and genre-appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do the Solars in your game currently do? </div> </div> </div>Combat/War, Preaching, Intelligence-gathering/social stuff, Social stuff/MA (that's actually a Lunar), Craft/Sorcery/Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I was playing a doctor, but I found it boring tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T09:20:59-08:00","id":1368052,"title":"","content":"A really good feature of the Ex3 Dragon-Blooded charmset is that signature charms have no prerequsites besides (ability) 5.<br /> It makes it very easy to wander into a support role at a fairly respectable level and do things that the Celestial Exalted whose already invested in it cannot. It is also worth remembering that at essence 5 you can double dip and learn a second signature charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T14:28:02-08:00","id":1368132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368051#post1368051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I shouldn't have used &quot;best&quot;. What I mean is about being useful to the group. I mean, I will take some combat stuff I think is cool, but no-one's going to go &quot;thank the Unconquered Sun we've got a combat-focused Dragonblood, or we'd be screwed!&quot; when most of the Solars are as good as a combat-focused Dragonblood, and one is much better.<br /> I don't want to feel like there's no reason for the other PCs to bother asking him to do anything, because they can do it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, realistically, there's almost never going to be a time where your circlemates are glad that you're a DB and not a Solar for practical reasons. From what I know of your campaign your group doesn't really care about cries of &quot;Anathema!&quot; there isn't a pervasive presence of the Immaculate Faith, there's no difficulty in wielding or aqurireing assets, and you're Essence 5 so being able to grab Essence 2/3 charms earlier than normal isn't a factor.<br /> <br /> So even if you go outside one of the other party member's niches you might not feel so great. Unless your ST is willing to let you have hundreds of descendants like a house matriarch or something.<br /> <br /> Your only other option really is to do cool shit that the Solars can't do, but probably isn't as effective as the stuff you'd be able to do as a Solar.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368051#post1368051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat/War, Preaching, Intelligence-gathering/social stuff, Social stuff/MA (that's actually a Lunar), Craft/Sorcery/Necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot of niches already covered. Assuming the Intelligence-Gathering person is also heavy into Awareness, Stealth, Invesetigation and Larceny that leaves you with...maybe Sail, Bureaucracy, Linguistics, Ride maybe, and that's about it. Occult and Lore are cool but with a Solar Sorcerer I imagine those are pretty heavily invested in already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T17:49:37-08:00","id":1368186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368051#post1368051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I shouldn't have used &amp;quot;best&amp;quot;. What I mean is about being useful to the group. I mean, I will take some combat stuff I think is cool, but no-one's going to go &amp;quot;thank the Unconquered Sun we've got a combat-focused Dragonblood, or we'd be screwed!&amp;quot; when most of the Solars are as good as a combat-focused Dragonblood, and one is much better.<br /> I don't want to feel like there's no reason for the other PCs to bother asking him to do anything, because they can do it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this group might need challenges that require them to separate.<br /> <br /> Still, Archery had an Aura Duration power to let you reflexively clash ranged attacks made against allies without needing to aim, that can reap Initiative from weakened attacks and done as many times as required per round. Also a decisive undodgeable attack that can be made on multiple opponents that rolls your <b>full</b> Initiative against each struck enemy. I'd say those would be assets even to Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can? Which charm is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Signature Wood one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T02:03:44-08:00","id":1368492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368186#post1368186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though this group might need challenges that require them to separate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That already happens, that already happens a lot, so much, every session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T02:10:45-08:00","id":1368495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362082-dragon-blooded-charm-vs-solar-charms?p=1368492#post1368492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That already happens, that already happens a lot, so much, every session.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What ? I don't care about this giant meteor threatening creation don't you see I'm finishing a working to make all the fish on Creation be slightly saltier when cooked ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T02:35:22-08:00","id":1368498,"title":"","content":"The last session actually we did mostly stick together (or at least, were on the same island) but now I think two-three characters are going to Varang to help them fight Harborhead, one's going to his own kingdom to investigate something there, and another is going to go and do some intelligence-gathering in another place.<br /> On the one hand, having 5-6 e5 Solars/Lunars in one place is overkill. On the other, it's a bit annoying when the party is split so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T03:50:49-08:00","id":1368508,"title":"","content":"Bureaucracy seems pretty solid for a Dragon-Blooded majordomo, with mounted archery as solid combat support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}